(version 1)
# L49b: the supply trial board's custom rules, copied next to the routed board
# by route.py (kicad-cli reads <board>.kicad_dru from the board's folder).
#
# Mains to everything else: the TRIAL reinforced creepage, 6.4 mm
# (make_board.py: the sources, and why the netclass cannot carry it). The
# placement keeps an empty band for it (place.py); this rule is what judges it.
(rule "mains_to_low_voltage"
  (constraint clearance (min 6.4mm))
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'MAINS' && B.NetClass != 'MAINS'"))

# Between two mains nets (L and N) the insulation is functional, and the
# source's footprints set it: the Phoenix MKDS 1,5 at 5.08 mm pitch leaves
# 2.48 mm pad to pad. The netclass carries 2.4 mm; the figure for L to N is
# G2's, with the norm (SAFETY.md) - here it is the footprint's, written down.
